WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.200
It: Chapter One scared the pants off of audiences
when it debuted in 2017, becoming the highest-grossing

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.260
horror movie of all time and leaving fans
hungry for more.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.140
And It: Chapter Two is certainly keeping pace
with its predecessor at the box office.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.900
According to the Los Angeles Times,

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.830
"[The film] scored $91 million in its first
weekend, making it the second-biggest horror

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.040
movie opening of all time, behind its 2017
predecessor."

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.460
"...Hello."

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.060
Together, the two films are likely to rake
in a worldwide box office take somewhere in

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.360
the neighborhood of $1.5 billion dollars.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.300
And this begs the question: Will there be
an It: Chapter Three?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.460
Please note: We'll be discussing a few plot
points from King's novel and the two films,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.589
so some spoilers are coming right at you!

00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:44.930
While both It movies were reasonably faithful
to the source material, Stephen King's epic

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.360
1986 novel of the same name, they weren't
completely so.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.820
Several set pieces solely appear in the films…like
Stan's run-in with the creepy lady from the

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.300
painting in the first film…and Bill's hall-of-mirrors
nightmare in the second.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.260
One of the most notable changes is the fact
that It: Chapter Two doesn't end with the

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.840
same city-destroying storm that concludes
the book.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.420
This difference could be telling.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:08.940
Following the success of It: Chapter One,
studio execs may have advised director Andy

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.540
Muschietti to leave the door open for a third
installment.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.140
But if that's the case, he certainly isn't
admitting it.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.320
In 2017, he did discuss the possibility of
splitting Chapter Two into seperate films,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.240
telling Variety:

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.460
"It would make sense because it would give
me more turf to develop the characters and

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.360
more of a canvas to develop the journey, but
to be honest, there wasn’t a conversation

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.520
about that and now we are designing the story
as one single film."

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.020
Of course, nothing motivates studio executives
like big bucks…and if New Line ultimately

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.980
decides to greenlight a third chapter, there's
a number of tracks the film could take.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.110
In fact, Pennywise actor Bill Skarsgård has
mentioned that he and Muschietti have kicked

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.300
around an idea for a third It movie.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.340
In a recent sitdown with JoBlo, the actor
opened up about those talks, saying that

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.480
"Andy and I have discussed ideas for what
a third movie would look like.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.520
I don't think it's quite what people expect.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.440
It's something different.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.240
The first two stories are the book, and the
second film is the end of that story.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.740
So we would do something quite literally off
book."

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.610
Skarsgård goes on to reveal that

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.640
"There are a few ideas floating around.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:09.280
I feel like I've done what I can with the
incarnation of Pennywise as we know of him,

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.080
so I think it would be a cool idea to change
up a few things.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.600
So, without going into too much detail, there
is a story that we're kind of excited about,

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.960
but it's way too early to say.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.340
But we'll see, we'll see."

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.360
The idea of a new "incarnation" of Pennywise
is certainly an intriguing one, although it's

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.120
safe to say there are about a million ways
to get that concept wrong.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:31.000
Obviously, any additions to King's masterpiece
would require a deft touch, but at least Muschietti

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.620
has already demonstrated his considerable
talent just by bringing It successfully to

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.460
the big screen.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.700
Of course, even if It: Chapter 3 never comes
to fruition, Pennywise could always return

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.160
to theaters in a supercut of the first two
films.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.220
And guess what?

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.220
Muschietti has definitely considered the idea,
as he recently told CinemaBlend:

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.840
"I am thinking of a supercut.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.500
Which is basically the two movies told one
after the other, adding everything that was

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.340
lifted from them for length purposes.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.420
Great scenes that are more character moments,
or things that we had to lift for other reasons.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.140
I’m also very excited about shooting extra
material."

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.640
Well, that news should certainly put a smile
on your face.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:12.220
Of course, if that plan comes to fruition,
we hope we're given an intermission or two…because

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.780
watching an It supercut would certainly gobble
up a gargantuan amount of time.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.880
Considering that Muschietti has already put
this idea out in the public sphere, we're

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.900
thinking a supercut could actually happen.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.860
As to whether we'll ever really see an It:
Chapter Three, we suspect that the likelihood

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.680
is pretty slim.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.160
And all things considered, that's probably
for the best.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.840
The novel spins an epic and phenomenally terrifying
yarn…but expanding the story would almost

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.560
certainly do the book a disservice.

